# Packages-Desktop — GUI packages
# Installed after Base. Profile-specific desktop meta-package is first.
# niri + shani-shell: the AI desktop (shani-desktop-niri pulls the shell,
# greetd with first-boot setup, portals, and the native apps GNOME's own
# metapackage brings; the rest are Flatpaks).
shani-desktop-niri
# pipewire-audio provides ladspa-host, and naming it here is what stops
# pacman picking ardour (a full DAW) for swh-plugins' virtual ladspa-host
# dependency: only a package named on the pacstrap line settles a provider
# (see Packages-Base). PipeWire's own host runs the SC4 compressor without
# the DAW.
pipewire-audio
shani-accessibility
shani-fonts
shani-multimedia
shani-bluetooth
shani-peripherals
shani-printer
shani-scanner
shani-video
shani-video-guest
shani-cassini
shani-backup
# The preinstalled brain (Qwen3.5-2B, 1.28 GB): the assistant thinks
# at first boot without a download. See shani-llm-model's PKGBUILD.
shani-llm-model
# shani-chronoa itself depends on the minimal voice stack (shani-piper-tts,
# shani-piper-voice, shani-whisper-model), so they are not pinned here.
shani-chronoa
desktop-entry-hider

# Input methods and OCR data are not pinned here: shani-desktop-niri already
# depends on shani-input-fcitx5 (the only input method that speaks niri's
# input-method-v2) and tesseract-data-eng (Lens reads text at first boot;
# other languages are downloaded by the setup wizard).
